# Drafted by Gemini (R14 maric), edited.

~ start
Narrator: A knight in a crisp crimson tabard stands pressed against the far wall, three yards clear of the watering trough and the black mare drinking from it.
ser_maric_dunmore [sly]: Hold there, pilgrims, and mind my sightlines. I am Ser Maric Dunmore, and I have taken this post by the wall for purely tactical reasons.
ser_maric_dunmore [neutral]: A true commander never crowds his mount before the horn sounds. Distance breeds discipline.
* Tell us about the Sanguine Hunt. -> maric_hunt
* You seem wary of the horses. -> maric_horses
* [Persuasion DC 12] Offer to help him with the horse -> maric_help | maric_nope
* [if flag.maric_helped] Ask him to loosen his saddle for us -> maric_deal
* Leave him to his post. -> END

~ maric_hunt
ser_maric_dunmore [smile]: We ride at the Twilight bell, the night after the courtyard pyres go cold. No sinner on the moor outruns the Crimson Rose.
ser_maric_dunmore [neutral]: Naturally, I command the rear guard. From the very back, a seasoned officer has full visibility of the field.
set hunt_known
-> start

~ maric_horses
Narrator: The mare lifts her dripping muzzle from the trough and fixes him with one wet, dark eye. His gauntlet tightens on his belt.
ser_maric_dunmore [afraid]: Horses are an unreliable tactical asset. Too many teeth at one end, iron shoes at the other, and no respect for rank.
ser_maric_dunmore [angry]: Look at her. She is calculating the angle right now.
-> start

~ maric_help
Narrator: You take the mare's bridle and stroke her cold nose while Ser Maric climbs into the stirrup with both eyes pinched shut.
ser_maric_dunmore [weary]: There. Seated in the saddle, master of the beast. You have a passable grasp of stable drill, pilgrim.
ser_maric_dunmore [neutral]: Let us speak no more of the mounting maneuver.
set maric_helped
-> start

~ maric_nope
ser_maric_dunmore [angry]: Help? I need no help with a mere pack beast. I simply noticed a draft by the trough and relocated to the woodpile for better cover.
-> start

~ maric_deal
ser_maric_dunmore [sly]: Slip the buckle two notches before the charge? A clean tumble into the snowbank at the first gallop, and no dishonor on my name.
ser_maric_dunmore [afraid]: Done. My girth was faulty, the leather gave way, and you never breathed a word of it.
set maric_loosened
-> start
